---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Who is alive?" hint="A cluster runs for two minutes. One node crashes at 20 s and another freezes for a while at 60 s, like a garbage-collection pause. Choose how the nodes find out, and watch the cost and the mistakes.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>The default is <b>all-to-all heartbeats</b>, a <b>3 s</b> timeout, <b>64 nodes</b> and <b>5%</b> packet loss. The crash is known after <b>3 s</b>, but <b>3 healthy nodes</b> are declared dead: the frozen node, because its <b>6 s</b> pause is longer than the timeout, and two more because of lost packets. Each node sends <b>62 messages a second</b>, and the false alarm moves <b>284 keys</b> out and back for nothing.</li>
    <li>Switch to <b>SWIM</b> and set the timeout to <b>8 s</b>: the crash is known to all after <b>10 s</b>, <b>no healthy node</b> is declared dead because the frozen node refutes its suspicion with a higher incarnation, and each node sends only <b>3 messages a second</b>. At <b>3 s</b> SWIM fails too, because the pause is longer than the suspicion time.</li>
    <li>Go back to heartbeats and choose <b>256 nodes</b>: each node sends <b>254 messages a second</b>, and the cost grows with the cluster. Back at <b>64 nodes</b>, <b>gossip</b> costs 3 messages a second, but with a <b>3 s</b> timeout it wrongly kills <b>63 of 63</b> nodes, because news arrives late and unevenly, and at <b>6 s</b> only 2. With gossip, <b>phi accrual</b> at threshold <b>8</b> makes no mistakes but takes <b>42 s</b> to notice the crash, and at <b>4</b> it takes <b>23 s</b>.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg cmb" data-cmb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Protocol <select class="pg-in" data-proto>
        <option value="a2a" selected>All-to-all heartbeats</option>
        <option value="gossip">Gossip heartbeats</option>
        <option value="swim">SWIM probes with suspicion</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Detector <select class="pg-in" data-det>
        <option value="fixed" selected>Fixed timeout</option>
        <option value="phi">Phi accrual</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Nodes <select class="pg-in" data-n>
        <option value="16">16</option>
        <option value="64" selected>64</option>
        <option value="256">256</option>
      </select></label>
      <label><span data-thrlabel>Silence before a node is declared dead (seconds)</span> <input type="range" min="1" max="15" value="3" data-thr /> <b data-thrval></b></label>
      <label>Packet loss (%) <input type="range" min="0" max="10" value="5" data-loss /> <b data-lossval></b></label>
      <label>Frozen node pause (seconds, 0 for none) <input type="range" min="0" max="30" value="6" data-pause /> <b data-pauseval></b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Time until every node knows of the crash</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Healthy nodes declared dead</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Messages per node per second</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Keys moved for nothing</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b5><h3>Requests sent to the wrong owner (worst moment)</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o5></span><span class="pg-note" data-n5></span></div>
    </div>
    <svg class="cmb-chart" viewBox="0 0 600 130" role="img" aria-label="Nodes that think the crashed node is dead over time" data-chart preserveAspectRatio="none">
      <rect class="cmb-pausebar" x="0" y="0" width="0" height="130" data-pausebar />
      <line class="cmb-grid" x1="0" y1="125" x2="600" y2="125" />
      <line class="cmb-grid" x1="0" y1="5" x2="600" y2="5" />
      <line class="cmb-mark" x1="100" y1="0" x2="100" y2="130" />
      <polyline class="cmb-line crash" points="" data-crashline />
      <polyline class="cmb-line slow" points="" data-slowline />
    </svg>
    <p class="pg-note">Chart, 0 to 120 s. Solid line: how many nodes think the crashed node is dead. Dashed line: how many think the frozen node is dead. Dotted vertical line: the crash at 20 s. Shaded band: the pause. The top of the chart is every node.</p>
    <div class="cmb-cells" data-cells role="img" aria-label="The cluster at the end of the run"></div>
    <p class="pg-note">Each square is a node at the end of the run: X is the crashed node, ! is a healthy node that at least one node declared dead at some point, and an empty square is a node that nobody ever accused.</p>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: one round per second, the same messages are lost with the chosen probability, and a frozen node neither sends nor answers but its network card still buffers what arrives. Heartbeats: every node sends to every other, and the detector fires when the silence exceeds the timeout. Gossip: each node bumps its own counter and sends its table to 3 random nodes, and a node is dead when it has not seen a peer's counter rise within the timeout. SWIM: each node pings one random peer per round and tries 3 indirect probes before suspecting it, updates (up to 24 per message) are piggybacked and each is sent 4 x ceil(log10 N+1) times, a suspect that hears of it refutes with a higher incarnation, and a suspect that stays silent for the timeout is dead. Phi accrual uses the exponential estimate phi = 0.434 x silence / mean interval. The ring has 16 virtual nodes per node and 10,000 keys, and it removes a node when more than half of the nodes consider it dead, then puts it back when they stop, so one needless removal moves its keys out and back. Wrong owner: the share of keys whose owner some node thinks is dead, weighted by how many nodes think so.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style is:global>
  .cmb-chart { width: 100%; height: 130px; display: block; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; }
  .cmb-grid { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; }
  .cmb-mark { stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 2 3; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; }
  .cmb-pausebar { fill: var(--accent-soft); }
  .cmb-line { fill: none; stroke-width: 2; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; }
  .cmb-line.crash { stroke: var(--bad); }
  .cmb-line.slow { stroke: var(--accent); stroke-dasharray: 6 4; }
  .cmb-cells { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, 18px); gap: 3px; }
  .cmb-cell { width: 18px; height: 18px; border: 1px solid var(--good); border-radius: 4px; font: .7rem/16px ui-monospace, monospace; text-align: center; color: var(--text); background: var(--surface); }
  .cmb-cell[hidden] { display: none; }
  .cmb-cell.crashed { background: var(--bad); border-color: var(--bad); color: var(--on-accent); }
  .cmb-cell.accused { border: 2px solid var(--bad); color: var(--bad-text); font-weight: 700; }
</style>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cmb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement | SVGElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    // SIM START
    const TICKS = 120, CRASH_T = 20, PAUSE_T = 60, C = 3, S = 9, KEYS = 10000, VN = 16, FAN = 3, K_IND = 3, PIG = 24;
    type Upd = { j: number; type: number; inc: number; left: number };
    type Params = { n: number; proto: string; det: string; thr: number; loss: number; pause: number };
    const EWMA_ALPHA = 0.1; // weight of the newest heartbeat gap in the mean
    const LOG10_E = 0.4342945; // phi for exponential gaps = (silence / mean) * log10(e)
    const RETRANSMIT_X = 4; // SWIM piggybacks each update 4 * log10(n + 1) times
    const MSG_BYTES = { header: 60, update: 16, counter: 12 }; // bytes per message, per piggybacked update, per gossiped counter
    const BYTES_PER_KB = 1000;
    // integer hash (murmur3-style finalizer)
    const mix = (x: number): number => { let h = Math.imul(x ^ 0x9e3779b9, 2246822519) >>> 0; h ^= h >>> 15; h = Math.imul(h, 3266489917) >>> 0; h ^= h >>> 13; h = Math.imul(h, 668265263) >>> 0; h ^= h >>> 16; return h >>> 0; };
    const ringCache: Record<number, number[]> = {};
    function ownership(n: number): number[] {
      if (ringCache[n]) return ringCache[n];
      const toks: [number, number][] = [];
      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) for (let v = 0; v < VN; v++) toks.push([mix(i * 1000 + v + 77), i]);
      toks.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]);
      const owned = new Array<number>(n).fill(0);
      for (let k = 0; k < KEYS; k++) {
        const h = mix(k * 7919 + 13); let lo = 0, hi = toks.length;
        while (lo < hi) { const m = (lo + hi) >> 1; if (toks[m][0] < h) lo = m + 1; else hi = m; }
        owned[toks[lo % toks.length][1]]++;
      }
      return (ringCache[n] = owned);
    }
    function simulate(p: Params) {
      const { n, proto, det, thr, loss, pause } = p;
      let seed = 12345 + n;
      const rnd = (): number => { // mulberry32
        seed = (seed + 0x6D2B79F5) | 0; let t = Math.imul(seed ^ (seed >>> 15), 1 | seed); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; };
      const lost = (): boolean => rnd() < loss;
      const crashed = (x: number, t: number): boolean => x === C && t >= CRASH_T;
      const paused = (x: number, t: number): boolean => x === S && t >= PAUSE_T && t < PAUSE_T + pause;
      const running = (x: number, t: number): boolean => !crashed(x, t) && !paused(x, t);
      const view = new Uint8Array(n * n); // 0 alive, 1 suspect, 2 dead
      const owned = ownership(n);
      let msgs = 0, bytes = 0, accus = 0, detectAt = -1, maxMis = 0, ringEvents = 0, moved = 0;
      const flagged = new Uint8Array(n), ringOut = new Uint8Array(n);
      const crashSeen: number[] = [], slowSeen: number[] = [];
      const last = new Int32Array(n * n), mean = new Float64Array(n * n).fill(1), cnt = new Int32Array(n * n);
      const hit = (o: number, j: number, t: number) => { const a = o * n + j; const gap = t - last[a]; if (gap > 0) mean[a] = Math.max(1, (1 - EWMA_ALPHA) * mean[a] + EWMA_ALPHA * gap); last[a] = t; };
      const isDead = (o: number, j: number, t: number): boolean => { const el = t - last[o * n + j]; return det === 'phi' ? (el / mean[o * n + j]) * LOG10_E > thr : el > thr; };
      const judge = (o: number, t: number) => {
        for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) if (j !== o) {
          const a = o * n + j; const d = isDead(o, j, t) ? 2 : 0;
          if (d === 2 && view[a] !== 2 && j !== C) { accus++; flagged[j] = 1; }
          view[a] = d;
        }
      };
      // SWIM state
      const known = new Int32Array(n * n), since = new Int32Array(n * n), selfInc = new Int32Array(n), refute = new Uint8Array(n);
      const buf: Upd[][] = Array.from({ length: n }, () => []);
      const R = RETRANSMIT_X * Math.ceil(Math.log10(n + 1));
      const perm = Array.from({ length: n }, () => ({ list: [] as number[], i: 0 }));
      const enqueue = (x: number, j: number, type: number, inc: number) => { const e = buf[x].find((u) => u.j === j); if (e) { e.type = type; e.inc = inc; e.left = R; } else buf[x].push({ j, type, inc, left: R }); };
      const apply = (x: number, j: number, type: number, inc: number, t: number) => {
        if (j === x) { if (type !== 0 && inc >= selfInc[x]) refute[x] = 1; return; }
        const a = x * n + j;
        if (type === 0) { if (inc > known[a]) { view[a] = 0; known[a] = inc; enqueue(x, j, 0, inc); } }
        else if (type === 1) { if (view[a] !== 2 && (inc > known[a] || (inc === known[a] && view[a] === 0))) { view[a] = 1; known[a] = inc; since[a] = t; enqueue(x, j, 1, inc); } }
        else if (view[a] !== 2 && inc >= known[a]) { view[a] = 2; known[a] = inc; enqueue(x, j, 2, inc); }
      };
      const take = (x: number): Upd[] => { const b = buf[x].sort((u, v) => v.left - u.left || u.j - v.j).slice(0, PIG); b.forEach((u) => u.left--); buf[x] = buf[x].filter((u) => u.left > 0); return b; };
      const send = (from: number, to: number, t: number): boolean => {
        msgs++; const pg = take(from);
        const a0 = from * n + to; if (view[a0] === 1 && !pg.some((u) => u.j === to)) pg.unshift({ j: to, type: 1, inc: known[a0], left: 0 }); // buddy system: tell a suspect that it is suspected
        bytes += MSG_BYTES.header + MSG_BYTES.update * pg.length;
        if (lost()) return false;
        pg.forEach((u) => apply(to, u.j, u.type, u.inc, t));
        return true;
      };
      for (let t = 0; t < TICKS; t++) {
        if (proto === 'a2a') {
          for (let s = 0; s < n; s++) if (running(s, t)) for (let o = 0; o < n; o++) if (o !== s) { msgs++; bytes += MSG_BYTES.header; if (!lost() && !crashed(o, t)) hit(o, s, t); }
          for (let o = 0; o < n; o++) if (running(o, t)) judge(o, t);
        } else if (proto === 'gossip') {
          for (let s = 0; s < n; s++) if (running(s, t)) { cnt[s * n + s]++; last[s * n + s] = t; }
          const snap = cnt.slice();
          for (let s = 0; s < n; s++) if (running(s, t)) for (let f = 0; f < FAN; f++) {
            let o = Math.floor(rnd() * (n - 1)); if (o >= s) o++;
            msgs++; bytes += MSG_BYTES.header + MSG_BYTES.counter * n;
            if (lost() || crashed(o, t)) continue;
            for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) { const v = snap[s * n + j]; const a = o * n + j; if (v > cnt[a]) { cnt[a] = v; hit(o, j, t); } }
          }
          for (let o = 0; o < n; o++) if (running(o, t)) judge(o, t);
        } else {
          for (let x = 0; x < n; x++) if (running(x, t) && refute[x]) { refute[x] = 0; selfInc[x]++; enqueue(x, x, 0, selfInc[x]); }
          for (let o = 0; o < n; o++) {
            if (!running(o, t)) continue;
            const pm = perm[o];
            if (pm.i >= pm.list.length) { pm.list = []; for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) if (j !== o && view[o * n + j] !== 2) pm.list.push(j); for (let i = pm.list.length - 1; i > 0; i--) { const k = Math.floor(rnd() * (i + 1)); [pm.list[i], pm.list[k]] = [pm.list[k], pm.list[i]]; } pm.i = 0; }
            let tg = -1; while (pm.i < pm.list.length) { const c = pm.list[pm.i++]; if (view[o * n + c] !== 2) { tg = c; break; } }
            if (tg < 0) continue;
            let ok = send(o, tg, t) && running(tg, t) && send(tg, o, t);
            if (!ok) {
              const cand: number[] = []; for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) if (j !== o && j !== tg && view[o * n + j] !== 2) cand.push(j);
              for (let k = 0; k < K_IND && cand.length; k++) {
                const m = cand.splice(Math.floor(rnd() * cand.length), 1)[0];
                if (send(o, m, t) && running(m, t) && send(m, tg, t) && running(tg, t) && send(tg, m, t) && send(m, o, t)) ok = true;
              }
              if (!ok) apply(o, tg, 1, known[o * n + tg], t);
            }
          }
          for (let o = 0; o < n; o++) if (running(o, t)) for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) { const a = o * n + j; if (view[a] === 1 && t - since[a] >= thr) { view[a] = 2; enqueue(o, j, 2, known[a]); if (j !== C) { accus++; flagged[j] = 1; } } }
        }
        let cs = 0, ss = 0, mis = 0;
        for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) {
          let dc = 0, obs = 0;
          for (let o = 0; o < n; o++) if (o !== j && !crashed(o, t)) { obs++; if (view[o * n + j] === 2) dc++; }
          if (j === C) { cs = dc; if (detectAt < 0 && t >= CRASH_T && dc === obs) detectAt = t - CRASH_T; continue; }
          if (j === S) ss = dc;
          mis += (owned[j] / KEYS) * (dc / (n - 1));
          const out = dc > (n - 1) / 2 ? 1 : 0;
          if (out && !ringOut[j]) { ringEvents++; moved += owned[j]; }
          if (!out && ringOut[j]) moved += owned[j];
          ringOut[j] = out;
        }
        maxMis = Math.max(maxMis, mis);
        crashSeen.push(cs); slowSeen.push(ss);
      }
      let wrong = 0; for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) wrong += flagged[j];
      return { detect: detectAt, wrong, accus, msgsPerNode: msgs / n / TICKS, kbPerNode: bytes / n / TICKS / BYTES_PER_KB, ringEvents, moved, maxMis, crashSeen, slowSeen, flagged };
    }
    // SIM END

    const MAXN = 256;
    // All-to-all is O(n^2) per round, so it is simulated with at most A2A_MAX nodes to keep the page responsive.
    // Its message cost does not depend on chance, so it is computed exactly for the chosen size.
    const A2A_MAX = 64;
    const CACHE_MAX = 40; // simulated results kept before the cache is cleared
    const MISROUTE_OK = 0.0005; // misrouted share below this counts as healthy
    const CHART = { xPerTick: 5, y0: 125, h: 120 }; // svg px
    const a2aCost = (n: number, pause: number) => { let s = 0; for (let t = 0; t < TICKS; t++) s += n - (t >= CRASH_T ? 1 : 0) - (t >= PAUSE_T && t < PAUSE_T + pause ? 1 : 0); const msgs = s * (n - 1); return { msgsPerNode: msgs / n / TICKS, kbPerNode: (msgs * MSG_BYTES.header) / n / TICKS / BYTES_PER_KB }; };
    const cells = q('[data-cells]');
    for (let i = 0; i < MAXN; i++) { const c = document.createElement('div'); c.className = 'cmb-cell'; cells.append(c); }
    const cellEls = Array.from(cells.children) as HTMLElement[];
    const sel = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s).value;
    const num = (s: string) => Number(q<HTMLInputElement>(s).value);
    const fmt = (v: number) => Math.round(v).toLocaleString('en-US');
    const cache = new Map<string, ReturnType<typeof simulate>>();
    let mode = '';
    function setMode() {
      const proto = sel('[data-proto]'); const phi = proto !== 'swim' && sel('[data-det]') === 'phi';
      const key = proto === 'swim' ? 'swim' : phi ? 'phi' : 'fixed';
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-det]').disabled = proto === 'swim';
      if (key === mode) return;
      mode = key;
      const thr = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-thr]'); thr.max = phi ? '12' : '15';
      if (Number(thr.value) > Number(thr.max)) thr.value = thr.max;
    }
    function draw() {
      setMode();
      const proto = sel('[data-proto]'); const det = proto === 'swim' ? 'fixed' : sel('[data-det]'); const n = Number(sel('[data-n]'));
      const thr = num('[data-thr]'); const loss = num('[data-loss]') / 100; const pause = num('[data-pause]');
      q('[data-thrval]').textContent = det === 'phi' ? `phi ${thr} (about ${Math.round(thr / LOG10_E)} s of silence on a steady link)` : `${thr} s`;
      q('[data-thrlabel]').textContent = proto === 'swim' ? 'Suspicion timeout (seconds)' : det === 'phi' ? 'Phi threshold' : 'Silence before a node is declared dead (seconds)';
      q('[data-lossval]').textContent = `${Math.round(loss * 100)}%`; q('[data-pauseval]').textContent = pause === 0 ? 'none' : `${pause} s`;
      const simN = proto === 'a2a' ? Math.min(n, A2A_MAX) : n;
      const key = [proto, det, simN, thr, loss, pause].join('|');
      let r = cache.get(key);
      if (!r) { r = simulate({ n: simN, proto, det, thr, loss, pause }); if (cache.size > CACHE_MAX) cache.clear(); cache.set(key, r); }
      const cost = simN < n ? a2aCost(n, pause) : r;
      const healthy = simN - 1; const slowFlag = r.flagged[S] === 1; const otherWrong = r.wrong - (slowFlag ? 1 : 0);
      const maxSlow = Math.max(...r.slowSeen);
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = r.detect >= 0 ? `${r.detect} s` : 'not by the end';
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = proto === 'a2a' ? 'Every node decides alone, once it has heard nothing for the timeout.' : proto === 'gossip' ? 'A node must also receive the news that the counter stopped rising, and the news arrives late and unevenly.' : 'First a probe fails, then the suspicion timeout runs, then the news is spread on the probe messages.';
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${r.wrong} of ${healthy}`;
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = `${fmt(r.accus)} accusations in all. ${pause > 0 ? `The frozen node was called dead by up to ${maxSlow} nodes.` : 'No node was frozen.'}`;
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = cost.msgsPerNode.toFixed(1);
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = `${cost.kbPerNode.toFixed(1)} KB/s out of each node, ${fmt(cost.msgsPerNode * n)} messages a second in the whole cluster.`;
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = `${fmt(r.moved)} of ${fmt(KEYS)} (${(r.moved / (KEYS / 100)).toFixed(1)}%)`;
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = r.ringEvents > 0 ? `${r.ringEvents} needless removal${r.ringEvents > 1 ? 's' : ''} from the ring, with the keys moved out and back.` : 'The ring was never changed for a healthy node.';
      q('[data-o5]').textContent = `${(r.maxMis * 100).toFixed(1)}%`;
      q('[data-n5]').textContent = 'Share of requests sent away from a healthy owner, because some nodes believe it is dead.';
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', r.detect >= 0 ? 'var(--accent)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', r.wrong === 0 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b4]').style.setProperty('--c', r.ringEvents === 0 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b5]').style.setProperty('--c', r.maxMis < MISROUTE_OK ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      const px = (t: number) => (t * CHART.xPerTick).toFixed(0); const py = (v: number) => (CHART.y0 - (v / healthy) * CHART.h).toFixed(1);
      q('[data-crashline]').setAttribute('points', r.crashSeen.map((v, t) => `${px(t)},${py(v)}`).join(' '));
      q('[data-slowline]').setAttribute('points', r.slowSeen.map((v, t) => `${px(t)},${py(v)}`).join(' '));
      const bar = q('[data-pausebar]'); bar.setAttribute('x', String(PAUSE_T * CHART.xPerTick)); bar.setAttribute('width', String(pause * CHART.xPerTick));
      q('[data-chart]').setAttribute('aria-label', `Nodes that think the crashed node is dead: ${r.crashSeen[TICKS - 1]} of ${healthy} at the end. Nodes that think the frozen node is dead: at most ${maxSlow}.`);
      cellEls.forEach((el, i) => {
        el.hidden = i >= simN;
        const state = i === C ? 'crashed' : r!.flagged[i] === 1 ? 'accused' : '';
        el.className = `cmb-cell ${state}`.trim(); el.textContent = state === 'crashed' ? 'X' : state === 'accused' ? '!' : '';
        el.title = `node ${i + 1}: ${state === 'crashed' ? 'crashed' : state === 'accused' ? 'healthy but declared dead' : 'never accused'}`;
      });
      cells.setAttribute('aria-label', `The cluster at the end of the run: 1 crashed node and ${r.wrong} healthy nodes that were declared dead.`);
      const out = q('[data-verdict]');
      const crashText = r.detect >= 0 ? `The crash at ${CRASH_T} s was known to all ${healthy} other nodes after ${r.detect} s.` : 'The crash had not reached every node by the end of the run.';
      const slowText = pause > 0 ? (slowFlag ? `The frozen node, paused ${pause} s, was declared dead by up to ${maxSlow} nodes.` : `The frozen node, paused ${pause} s, was never declared dead.`) : '';
      const lossText = otherWrong > 0 ? `${otherWrong} other healthy node${otherWrong > 1 ? 's were' : ' was'} accused only because packets were lost.` : '';
      const ringText = r.ringEvents > 0 ? `The ring moved ${fmt(r.moved)} keys for nothing.` : 'No data was moved for a healthy node.';
      const capText = simN < n ? `All-to-all heartbeats are simulated with ${simN} nodes here to keep the page responsive, so every result except the message cost is for ${simN} nodes; the message cost is for all ${n}.` : '';
      out.textContent = [crashText, r.wrong === 0 ? 'No healthy node was declared dead.' : `${r.wrong} healthy node${r.wrong > 1 ? 's were' : ' was'} declared dead.`, slowText, lossText, ringText, capText].filter(Boolean).join(' ');
      out.classList.toggle('bad', r.wrong > 0 || r.detect < 0);
    }
    let queued = false;
    const schedule = () => { if (queued) return; queued = true; requestAnimationFrame(() => { queued = false; draw(); }); };
    root.addEventListener('input', schedule); root.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    draw();
  });
</script>
